                <pb facs="0416" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-10-10T20:00:00-05:00">October 10, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>385. The next meeting of the Governing Body of the High Commission for German
                    Refugees is to be held in London on November 2 and 3. Inasmuch as it is the
                    practice of this Government to be officially represented at these meetings and
                    as it is impracticable to send anyone from here on this occasion, I should
                    appreciate your acting as American representative at the coming London meeting.
                    Though it is understood that in the case of certain other States representatives
                    of high diplomatic rank have attended Governing Body meetings, it will doubtless
                    suffice if you present yourself at the opening of the first session, thereafter
                    leaving attendance to Johnson or any other member of your staff that you choose
                    to designate to report the proceedings promptly and accurately. Written
                    instruction follows.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d253-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
